Program Bug_2_72_IncludeResolutionCwd;
// Bug 2.72: `@include` inside a `.tru` unit only resolves its
// units/<SYSTEM>/.../units/cpu_specific/<PROCESSOR>/... fallback paths
// correctly when the compiler is invoked with the repo root as the
// current working directory. Parser::HandleUseTPU (@use's .tru lookup)
// anchors its search dirs with Util::GetSystemPrefix(), which resolves
// relative to wherever the compiler binary lives, regardless of cwd.
// Parser::PreprocessIncludeFiles (@include's fallback lookup, reached
// once the local-directory check fails) instead anchors its fallback
// paths with the always-empty Util::path, so on Linux the fallback is
// silently relative to the process's CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY instead -
// this only "works" by coincidence when cwd happens to be the repo root
// (where a real units/ directory happens to sit at that relative path).
//
// units/C64/output/pbm.tru (@use "output/pbm") does `@include
// "output/pbm/macro.ras"` right after its var block opens, making it a
// minimal real-world trigger for this bug: it needs no PBM setup beyond
// the 5 @define values the unit itself requires before it'll even parse
// that far.
//
// Method B (compile-time), no VICE step, and CWD-DEPENDENT: run
// run_regressions.sh normally (it cd's into this folder, NOT the repo
// root), so this reproduces the documented pre-fix failure exactly as
// filed: "Could not open file for inclusion:
// units/cpu_specific/MOS6502/output/pbm/macro.ras" (the file genuinely
// exists, just at units/C64/output/pbm/macro.ras instead - the SYSTEM-dir
// fallback attempt failed the same cwd-relative way just before this,
// final one shown is the last one tried). Confirmed live: invoking the
// identical file from the repo root instead gets past this error
// entirely and fails later for an unrelated, expected reason (this
// snippet does no real PBM initialization). Post-fix, once
// PreprocessIncludeFiles's fallback paths anchor to
// Util::GetSystemPrefix() like HandleUseTPU already does, this should hit
// that same later, cwd-independent failure regardless of where the
// compiler is invoked from - proving the fix, not full PBM correctness.

var

@define PBMADDRESS $0400
@define PBMDISPLAYWIDTH 40
@define PBMSCREENWIDTH 40
@define PBMBUFFERWIDTH 40
@define PBMBUFFERHEIGHT 25

@use "output/pbm"

begin
	loop();
end.
